00:04:14.266 --> 00:04:15.799
- [Voiceover] Nikhil
asks, what do you think

00:04:15.799 --> 00:04:19.880
of Twitter's plan to remove
the 140 character limit?

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.267
- Nikhil, I think this is a
tremendous execution by Twitter.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:25.239
Twitter really needs a
jumpstart in a lot of ways,

00:04:25.239 --> 00:04:27.282
and really the reason it had a limit,

00:04:27.282 --> 00:04:29.813
was because of the technology in place.

00:04:29.813 --> 00:04:32.785
Because it was really in
the old 160-character limit

00:04:32.785 --> 00:04:35.223
or something of that nature
with the phone structure,

00:04:35.223 --> 00:04:38.195
of text, and like, there's
no reason at this point

00:04:38.195 --> 00:04:39.240
to keep that limit.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.724
It created creativity, I
think it served a purpose,

00:04:41.724 --> 00:04:43.442
but you gotta evolve or die,

00:04:43.442 --> 00:04:45.695
and I think the freedom of more characters

00:04:45.695 --> 00:04:46.507
could be helpful.

00:04:46.507 --> 00:04:48.365
Plus you have a lot of base of people

00:04:48.365 --> 00:04:49.549
over the last eight years that use it

00:04:49.549 --> 00:04:52.237
that will still keep
things short and tight.

00:04:52.237 --> 00:04:54.945
For me, I can see us now
doing complete blog post

00:04:54.945 --> 00:04:56.380
type things, like we do on Facebook,

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.443
in a Twitter environment.

00:04:57.443 --> 00:04:59.069
Could open up some opportunity.

00:04:59.069 --> 00:05:02.226
I think this is a very smart
move, a much-needed move,

00:05:02.226 --> 00:05:05.477
